WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.750
Hi, I'm Abhijit Verekar.

2
00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:05.490
I wrote Start at Zero, and I'm the
founder and CEO of Avero Advisors,

3
00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:09.140
where for nearly 20 years we've been
helping governments and universities

4
00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:13.097
make better decisions about enterprise
systems, and these days about AI,

5
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.950
and now I also spend time speaking
and investing in a few

6
00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:18.550
companies that I believe in.

7
00:00:18.733 --> 00:00:23.700
Most of what I talk about is government
ERP, ERP in general, and AI

8
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.960
modernization, and how to do it well,

9
00:00:26.167 --> 00:00:30.547
because in my experience, the projects
that work are the ones where somebody

10
00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:35.637
owned the decision and proved that
data was ready before the first demo,

11
00:00:35.907 --> 00:00:39.807
rather than replacing system A for
system B and getting stuck doing the

12
00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:42.307
same old workflows in a new product.

13
00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:46.633
In my speaking engagements, I give
a room something they can use on

14
00:00:46.643 --> 00:00:48.933
Monday, than another vendor tour,

15
00:00:49.013 --> 00:00:53.583
so people will leave with a phase zero
checklist and language that they can

16
00:00:53.593 --> 00:00:57.433
take straight into their next
leadership meeting, along with a better sense

17
00:00:57.443 --> 00:01:01.763
of which questions to ask before they
sign anything that's hard to walk back.

18
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.720
So if you're putting together an event
for public sector leaders and you think

19
00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:09.640
this would be useful to your audience,
send me a note through the form here

20
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:13.300
on the Speaking page or reach out to
me on LinkedIn, and I'll get back to

21
00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:16.870
you so we can have a real conversation
about what your audience needs.

22
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:17.767
Thank you.

